        "create_time": 1738574182.267883,
        "update_time": null,
        "content": {
          "content_type": "text",
          "parts": [
            "**Pyroid3** is an Android app that allows you to run **Python 3** scripts directly on your device. It's useful for testing, learning, and small-scale development without needing a PC. Here's how to operate it:\n\n---\n\n### **1. Installing Pyroid3**\n- Download **Pyroid3** from the Google Play Store or an APK provider.\n- Install and open the app.\n\n---\n\n### **2. Setting Up Pyroid3**\n- The app provides a built-in **Python interpreter** and **terminal**.\n- If required, install additional modules via **pip** (Pyroid3 supports it).\n  - Example: `pip install numpy`\n\n---\n\n### **3. Running Python Scripts**\n- Open **Pyroid3**.\n- Use the built-in **editor** to write Python scripts.\n- Tap the **Run** button to execute the script.\n- Alternatively, use the **terminal** to run scripts manually:\n  ```sh\n  python my_script.py\n  ```\n\n---\n\n### **4. Managing Dependencies**\n- Install additional packages using:\n  ```sh\n  pip install package_name\n  ```\n- Some modules may require manual setup due to Android restrictions.\n\n---\n\n### **5. File Management**\n- Store and access Python scripts from:\n  - Internal storage: `/storage/emulated/0/`\n  - App directory\n- Use the `os` module to navigate directories:\n  ```python\n  import os\n  print(os.listdir(\"/storage/emulated/0/\"))\n  ```\n\n---\n\n### **6. Limitations**\n- Some system-level libraries may not work due to Android restrictions.\n- Performance is limited compared to running Python on a PC.\n\n---\n\nWould you like guidance on a specific feature or use case?"
          ]
        },
