        "create_time": 1738574675.703053,
        "update_time": null,
        "content": {
          "content_type": "text",
          "parts": [
            "To pull up your saved Python file in **Pyroid3** and edit it, follow these steps:  \n\n### **1. Open Pyroid3**\n- Launch the **Pyroid3** app on your Android device.\n\n### **2. Locate Your File**\n- If you saved your script in **internal storage**, navigate to:  \n  `/storage/emulated/0/`  \n- If saved inside a specific folder, find it using the file manager.\n\n### **3. Open the File in Pyroid3**\n- In Pyroid3, tap the **menu (three dots or folder icon)**.  \n- Choose **\"Open\"** or **\"Open File\"**.  \n- Navigate to the folder where you saved your file.  \n- Select your **`.py`** file to open and edit it.\n\n### **4. Edit and Save**\n- Modify the script as needed.  \n- Tap **\"Save\"** (usually found in the menu).  \n\n### **5. Run Your Script**\n- Press the **Run** button to test changes.  \n- Alternatively, open the **terminal** and run:  \n  ```sh\n  python your_script.py\n  ```\n\nWould you like help with debugging or running your script?"
          ]
